- Commits done to this project should respect the following:

    [type]([scope]):[commit message]

    Examples:   "feat(main): Added a new window"
                "chore: Changed folder structure"
                "docs: Updated README"

    - [type] = The type of commit done. Examples include: feat = feature, fix = fixes, docs = documentation etc.
    - (optional) [scope] = The areas where changes have been made. This can either be an entire module or a single file.
    - [commit message] = A short text that explains what has changed.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Branches created should be named as:

    [owner]/[type]/[functionality]

    Examples:   "VD/feat/player-movement"
                "VornicuDavid/feat/spells"
                "BC/fix/spells"

    - [owner] = Either full name or abreviated.
    - [type] = The type of implementation done: features, fixes, etc.
    - [functionality] = Suggestive name for implementation. Check examples.
